    "backend_protocol": "HTTP/1.1 keep-alive",
    "response_body_bytes": 1048576,
    "aggregator_limit_bytes": 67108864,
    "load_balancing": "LeastConnectionsStrategy",
    "gateway_log_level": "WARN (com.vuhongquang.cache at INFO)",
    "k6_script": "bench-keyspace.js \u2014 random URI over a keyspace, uniform or Zipf",
    "notes": [
      "Uniform random access. Measured hit rate 12.8% matches theory exactly: 128 cached entries / 1000 keyspace = 12.8%. Under uniform access no eviction policy can beat the fraction of the keyspace held, since there is no locality to exploit.",
      "Keyspace test: requests spread over 1000 distinct URIs (/api/movies/0 .. /api/movies/999), each returning a 1 MB body. Working set ~1 GB against a 128 MB cache, so the cache holds ~128 entries and eviction runs constantly.",
      "Router.match uses uri::startsWith, so /api/movies/<n> routes to the movie pool without config changes; dummy_backend.py ignores the path and returns the same 1 MB body for every URI.",
      "Both backends served traffic: a verification run measured a 3806/3285 split across :8081 and :8082 under LeastConnectionsStrategy.",
      "Hit rate measured directly via ResponseCache.logStats(), scheduled every 10s in Main. Logback config put com.vuhongquang.cache at INFO and root at WARN so per-request logging did not distort throughput.",
      "Cache held its budget exactly throughout: 128 entries / 134217728 bytes on every stats line.",
      "NOT comparable to the 2026-08-05 single-URI run (3839.70 rps, ~100% hit rate): that one served one permanently-hot entry and never evicted. Throughput drops ~3x once the cache faces real pressure.",
      "Every cache miss copies the 1 MB body twice \u2014 once in ByteBufUtil.getBytes, once in CachedResponse's defensive clone. At a 12.8% hit rate that is ~2 MB of copying per request and is a known cost of the current design."
    ]
  },
